WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:05.460
Over the last few years, I've launched five
art competitions, and now the incredible art

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:08.160
from those competitions has a home.

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:09.160
Soul Arts.

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:15.009
A beautiful tome, carefully crafted, and full
of art inspired by Demon's Souls, Dark Souls,

00:00:15.009 --> 00:00:17.590
Bloodborne, Sekiro, and Elden Ring.

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:22.520
To be clear, the book has no official link
to these games, but that's exactly what makes

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:24.780
the art within so creative.

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:29.800
These artists imagined places, bosses, and
weapons, that have never been visualised before...expanding

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:34.010
the worlds that we love in an exceptional
way.

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:39.059
Go beyond the Sixth Archstone, and read about
the Twisted City, where the Weaver gently

00:00:39.059 --> 00:00:40.270
distorts the world..

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:45.640
Or skip ahead to the Unseen Lands, where artists
brought to life regions that we never got

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:47.019
to see in-game.

00:00:47.019 --> 00:00:52.769
Few would have seen this piece from the "Imagining
Bloodborne 2" competition, which depicts Caryll's

00:00:52.769 --> 00:00:54.089
terrible fate..

00:00:54.089 --> 00:00:59.679
Nor this piece of Prosthetic art, where Sekiro
becomes equipped with a Pivoting Greatsword.

00:00:59.679 --> 00:01:04.430
Then there's the chapter for Elden Ring..with
bosses and open worlds drawn from a time where

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:07.230
we knew absolutely nothing about the game.

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:13.510
So we'd be honoured if Soul Arts could earn
a place on your bookshelf, or coffee table.

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:18.330
This kickstarter is a real leap of faith,
but with your help, I know we can create something

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:20.370
that you'll come to treasure.

00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:22.660
Here's a preview of your reward tiers:

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:23.860
A digital edition.

00:01:23.860 --> 00:01:27.360
A cover art poster by Ricardo Emig.

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:28.740
The art book itself.

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:30.840
The art book with the slipcase..

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:33.760
An art exhibition bundle, featuring a collage
poster.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:38.140
The benefactor bundle, where your name will
be listed at the back of the book

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:40.680
And a signed edition, from me.

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:45.310
I'll be back at the end of the video..but
for now, I'm going to pass over to Jason,

00:01:45.310 --> 00:02:10.780
our publisher, who is going to explain things
in 

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:26.460
a 

00:02:26.460 --> 00:06:22.940
bit 

00:06:22.940 --> 00:11:22.579
more detail.

